## Type Declarations

### Strict Types

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Services;

// ✅ ALWAYS use strict types in new files
class MarketService
{
    // Type declarations for all parameters and return types
    public function calculateProbability(int $votes, int $totalVotes): float
    {
        if ($totalVotes === 0) {
            return 0.0;
        }

        return $votes / $totalVotes;
    }
}
```

### Return Type Declarations

```php
<?php

class MarketRepository
{
    // ✅ GOOD: Explicit return types
    public function findById(int $id): ?Market
    {
        return Market::find($id);
    }

    public function getActive(): Collection
    {
        return Market::where('status', MarketStatus::ACTIVE)->get();
    }

    public function exists(int $id): bool
    {
        return Market::where('id', $id)->exists();
    }

    public function delete(Market $market): void
    {
        $market->delete();
    }

    // ✅ Union return types
    public function findByIdentifier(int|string $id): Market|null
    {
        // Implementation
    }
}
```

### Property Type Declarations

```php
<?php

class Market extends Model
{
    // ✅ Typed properties
    protected string $table = 'markets';
