## Array Handling

### Array Destructuring

```php
<?php

// ✅ Array destructuring
[$name, $description, $category] = $this->parseMarketData($data);

// ✅ Associative array destructuring
['name' => $name, 'status' => $status] = $market;

// ✅ Nested destructuring
['user' => ['name' => $userName, 'email' => $email]] = $data;
```

### Spread Operator

```php
<?php

// ✅ Array spread operator
$defaults = ['status' => 'active', 'verified' => false];
$data = ['name' => 'Market 1', 'status' => 'pending'];

$merged = [...$defaults, ...$data];
// Result: ['status' => 'pending', 'verified' => false, 'name' => 'Market 1']

// ✅ Function argument unpacking
$numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
$max = max(...$numbers);
```

### Array Functions

```php
<?php

// ✅ Modern array methods
$markets = collect([
    ['name' => 'Market 1', 'volume' => 1000],
    ['name' => 'Market 2', 'volume' => 2000],
    ['name' => 'Market 3', 'volume' => 1500],
]);

// Filter
$highVolume = $markets->filter(fn($m) => $m['volume'] > 1200);

// Map
$names = $markets->map(fn($m) => $m['name']);

// Reduce
$totalVolume = $markets->reduce(fn($carry, $m) => $carry + $m['volume'], 0);

// Sort
$sorted = $markets->sortByDesc('volume');
```

## Arrow Functions

```php
<?php

// ✅ Arrow functions (PHP 7.4+)
$markets = Market::all();

// Short syntax for simple callbacks
$names = $markets->map(fn($market) => $market->name);

$active = $markets->filter(fn($market) => $market->status === MarketStatus::ACTIVE);

$volumes = $markets->map(fn($market) => [
    'name' => $market->name,
    'volume' => $market->calculateVolume(),
]);
```

## Null Coalescing

```php
<?php

// ✅ Null coalescing operator
$limit = $request->input('limit') ?? 20;
$category = $filters['category'] ?? 'all';

// ✅ Null coalescing assignment (PHP 7.4+)
$data['status'] ??= MarketStatus::ACTIVE;
$config['timeout'] ??= 30;

// ❌ OLD: Ternary with isset
$limit = isset($request->input('limit')) ? $request->input('limit') : 20;
```

## Code Formatting

### Method Chaining

```php
<?php

// ✅ GOOD: One method per line for readability
$markets = Market::query()
    ->where('status', MarketStatus::ACTIVE)
    ->where('end_date', '>', now())
    ->with(['creator', 'options'])
    ->orderBy('created_at', 'desc')
    ->paginate(20);

// ✅ Fluent interface formatting
$market = Market::create($data)
    ->load('options')
    ->refresh();
```

### Array Formatting

```php
<?php

// ✅ Multi-line arrays with trailing comma
$data = [
    'name' => 'Presidential Election',
    'description' => 'Will Trump win?',
    'category' => 'politics',
    'end_date' => '2024-11-05',
    'options' => [
        ['name' => 'Yes', 'probability' => 50],
        ['name' => 'No', 'probability' => 50],
    ],
];

// ✅ Short arrays on single line
$statuses = ['active', 'resolved', 'closed'];
```

## Security Best Practices

### SQL Injection Prevention

```php
<?php

// ✅ GOOD: Parameter binding (Eloquent/Query Builder)
$markets = Market::where('status', $status)->get();

// ✅ GOOD: Named bindings for raw queries
$markets = DB::select(
    'SELECT * FROM markets WHERE status = :status',
    ['status' => $status]
);

// ❌ BAD: String concatenation
$markets = DB::select("SELECT * FROM markets WHERE status = '$status'");
```

### Mass Assignment Protection

```php
<?php

class Market extends Model
{
    // ✅ GOOD: Explicitly define fillable fields
    protected $fillable = [
        'name',
        'description',
        'category',
        'end_date',
        'creator_id',
    ];

    // OR: Define guarded fields
    protected $guarded = [
        'id',
        'resolved_at',
        'resolution_value',
    ];
}
```

### XSS Prevention

```php
<?php

// ✅ In Blade templates, {{ }} automatically escapes
<h1>{{ $market->name }}</h1>

// ✅ Use {!! !!} only for trusted HTML
<div>{!! $trustedHtmlContent !!}</div>

// ✅ In PHP, use htmlspecialchars
echo htmlspecialchars($userInput, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8');
```

## Testing Standards

### PHPUnit Test Structure

```php
<?php

namespace Tests\Feature;

use App\Models\Market;
use App\Models\User;
use Illuminate\Foundation\Testing\RefreshDatabase;
use Tests\TestCase;

class MarketControllerTest extends TestCase
{
    use RefreshDatabase;

    /** @test */
    public function it_displays_list_of_markets(): void
    {
        // Arrange
        $markets = Market::factory()->count(3)->create();

        // Act
        $response = $this->get('/markets');

        // Assert
        $response->assertOk();
        $response->assertInertia(fn($page) =>
            $page->component('Markets/Index')
                ->has('markets.data', 3)
        );
    }

    /** @test */
    public function authenticated_user_can_create_market(): void
    {
        $user = User::factory()->create();

        $data = [
            'name' => 'Test Market',
            'description' => 'Test Description',
            'category' => 'politics',
            'end_date' => now()->addDays(30)->toDateTimeString(),
        ];

        $response = $this->actingAs($user)
            ->post('/markets', $data);

        $response->assertRedirect();
        $this->assertDatabaseHas('markets', [
            'name' => 'Test Market',
            'creator_id' => $user->id,
        ]);
    }
}
```

**Remember**: Modern PHP 8.2+ features enable cleaner, more type-safe code. Follow PSR standards, use Laravel conventions, and leverage PHP's latest features for maintainable applications.
